# scripts/lib/lychee-pin.env — sourced, never executed. One definition of each fact.
#
# Three consumers read this file and none of them restates it:
#   .github/workflows/validate.yml   (CI)
#   scripts/local-ci.sh              (local harness)
#   scripts/invariants/link-check-reaches-deep.sh   (the control)
# Two copies of a version string drifting apart is the failure this file exists to prevent.

# LYCHEE_VERSION IS LOAD-BEARING, NOT HOUSEKEEPING.
# `--exclude-path` is a REGEX, and it only became one in lychee v0.20.0 (2025-08-22, PR #1766).
# Below that release it is a plain PathBuf and the archive exclusion below is a SILENT NO-OP:
# nothing errors, the scan simply stops excluding. Do not lower this pin.
# (lychee issues #470, #1405, #1608.)
LYCHEE_VERSION=v0.24.2

# Fetched once from the upstream .sha256 sidecars and recorded HERE on purpose.
# Fetching the checksum from the same host as the binary proves nothing: whoever can replace
# one can replace the other. The pin in this repo is what makes verification mean something.
LYCHEE_SHA256_x86_64_linux=1f4e0ef7f6554a6ed33dd7ac144fb2e1bbed98598e7af973042fc5cd43951c9a
LYCHEE_SHA256_aarch64_darwin=c9d3740ea2d891854d37116c9fba840f37b6e7c89d330e7db84ac333631c4977

# --exclude-path skips the FILE being scanned. `.lycheeignore` and `--exclude` do NOT -- they
# match the LINK TARGET url, so neither can keep a directory out of the scan.
#
# WHY docs/archive/** IS EXCLUDED RATHER THAN REPAIRED: the retention drain moves bytes
# verbatim, so a broken link under docs/archive/ is a faithful record of a link that was
# already broken when it was archived. Archived bytes are never hand-edited.
# Repairing one would falsify history; excluding it is the only correct treatment.
#
# The value is a REGEX, not a glob. `docs/archive/**` would NOT work here.
LYCHEE_ARGS_COMMON="--no-progress --offline --include-fragments --exclude-path (^|/)docs/archive/"

# Quoted, and ./-prefixed. The glob crate requires a separator prefix for `**`
# (lychee-action PR #73, bug 2). Quoting ALONE is not the documented fix.
LYCHEE_TARGET="./**/*.md"

# LYCHEE_TARGET, EVEN QUOTED, DOES NOT REACH DOT-PREFIXED DIRECTORIES. Measured
# against the pinned lychee 0.24.2: `"$LYCHEE" $LYCHEE_ARGS_COMMON "$LYCHEE_TARGET"`
# silently skips every path with a dot-prefixed component -- `.claude/` is the one that matters
# here, and it can hold tracked .md files the scan must reach. This is
# lychee's own glob engine, not bash's: quoting bypasses bash entirely, and
# the miss survives it.
#
# `--hidden` ("Do not skip hidden directories and files") DOES make lychee reach them, and was
# tried first. REJECTED: with `--hidden` added to
# LYCHEE_ARGS_COMMON, --dump-inputs also takes in every gitignored tool-cache directory in the
# checkout (`.pytest_cache/` and the like). Combining with
# `--no-ignore=false` (the default) made no difference, because lychee's glob-based input
# discovery does not consult `.gitignore` at all in this invocation shape -- confirmed
# separately: a gitignored .md file that is not dot-prefixed is ALREADY
# reached by the plain LYCHEE_TARGET above, with no ignore-file consultation in play. `--hidden`
# is a single global toggle with no path scoping, so turning it on for the whole scan is not a
# surgical fix for one directory -- it is a standing invitation for every future
# gitignored dot-directory anyone creates in a checkout to join CI's link check silently.
#
# The surgical fix: lychee takes multiple positional inputs, so an EXPLICIT second target reaches
# `.claude/**/*.md` directly without touching the global hidden-file toggle at all.
# All three consumers of LYCHEE_TARGET pass this as a SECOND, separately quoted argument, never
# concatenated into LYCHEE_TARGET itself -- concatenating them into one string would have to be
# either unquoted (reintroducing the bash globstar-collapse bug the quoting removed) or quoted-as-one
# (which would hand lychee a single argument containing a literal space, matching nothing).
#
# If a tracked .md file ever appears under some OTHER dot-prefixed directory, this scan will
# silently miss it again -- the set-comparison assertion in link-check-reaches-deep.sh catches
# that when it happens, by set difference, not by trusting this comment to stay complete.
LYCHEE_TARGET_HIDDEN="./.claude/**/*.md"

# The pre-fix form, kept deliberately. It is DATA for the negative arm of
# scripts/invariants/link-check-reaches-deep.sh, not a leftover. Under bash, globstar is off
# by default, so `**` collapses to `*` and the scan never leaves the second path segment.
# Deleting this makes the control unable to prove it still measures anything.
LYCHEE_TARGET_SHALLOW='**/*.md'
